// Post-deployment identity app settings for one App Service site -- a Web App OR
// a Function App (both are 'Microsoft.Web/sites'). Generated by CruftFree. Do not
// edit manually.
//
// A Function App runs the same generated assemble_settings() as the web app, so
// it hard-requires the same CRUFTFREE_CALLER_* keys; main.bicep invokes this module
// once per function site too, passing the function app's name and baseAppSettings
// output (function apps receive the trusted-caller keys only -- no end-user
// identity audiences).
//
// SINGLE-WRITER INVARIANT: this module is the ONLY writer of this site's
// 'Microsoft.Web/sites/config@appsettings' resource besides the site module
// (web-app or function-app) that owns the base settings. Two modules declaring
// that same child resource do not merge -- the later deployment REPLACES the
// earlier one's properties, so a second leaf would silently drop these keys. Any
// future post-deployment app setting sourced from another module's output MUST be
// added to this module as a new param folded into the union() below, never as a
// sibling leaf module.
//
// It carries two independent groups, either of which may be absent:
//   1. Trusted-caller settings (DI-1/D14) -- present only under a managed gateway.
//   2. Late-bound end-user identity audiences -- the Entra app registration's
//      client-ID GUID, which Graph assigns at converge time and which therefore
//      cannot be baked into the static identity provider plan. The plan names the
//      env var in `allowedAudienceRefs`; this module supplies its value.
//
// WHY A SEPARATE LEAF MODULE (not app settings on the web-app module itself):
// the trusted-caller principal set is `{APIM system-MI principalId}` plus the
// principalId of every peer web app that `uses` this service. Those are
// post-creation identity outputs of OTHER modules (apiManagement + sibling
// web-app modules). Passing them as params to the web-app module would make the
// web app depend on APIM and on its peers -- and with mutual `uses` (A uses B,
// B uses A) that is an unbreakable BCP080 module cycle, and APIM already depends
// on every web app hostname. This module is a LEAF: main.bicep passes the
// cross-module expressions here, this module holds edges to APIM + peers + the
// target site, and NOTHING depends on this module -- so no cycle can form (the
// same leaf-grant pattern used for pooled RBAC role assignments).
//
// It applies the three settings AFTER the site (and every referenced identity)
// exists. The base app settings are threaded in AS DATA via the baseAppSettings
// param (from the web-app module baseAppSettings output); this module reproduces
// and overlays the three CRUFTFREE_CALLER_* keys. It does NOT read the site own
// settings at runtime: a self-read of this config resource own appsettings (the
// ARM listing function pointed at the appsettings child of this same site) inside
// this same config resource is a circular dependency ARM rejects at deploy time
// (InvalidTemplate: Circular dependency detected). Passing the base settings as
// data avoids that self-cycle.

@description('Name of the target App Service site -- a Web App or a Function App (its site resource already exists).')
param webAppName string

@description('Base app settings from the web-app module, overlaid with the keys below.')
param baseAppSettings array

@description('Trusted-caller backend audience client ID (DI-1/D14). Empty when the app has no managed gateway.')
param trustedCallerClientId string = ''

@description('Sovereign-cloud AAD token issuer for trusted callers (DI-1/D14).')
param trustedCallerExpectedIssuer string = ''

@description('Comma-separated trusted caller principal IDs (DI-1/D14): APIM system MI plus every peer web app that uses this service.')
param trustedCallerPrincipalIds string = ''

@description('Late-bound end-user identity audiences: IDENTITY_<PROVIDER>_AUDIENCE_CLIENT_ID -> the deploy-time client-ID GUID of the Entra app registration. Empty when the app declares no Entra end-user provider.')
param identityAudienceSettings object = {}

resource webApp 'Microsoft.Web/sites@2023-12-01' existing = {
  name: webAppName
}

// Emitting the CRUFTFREE_CALLER_* keys with empty values would be worse than
// omitting them: the runtime treats a present-but-empty trusted-caller audience
// as a configured-but-unsatisfiable check rather than "no managed gateway".
//
// The two halves of trusted-caller wiring are delivered independently, because a
// service may need either or both:
//   * OUTBOUND (attach my token when calling peers) needs ONLY the audience
//     client id -- an outbound-only caller (e.g. an async-only worker with `uses`
//     directives and no inbound surface) receives just that key.
//   * INBOUND (validate who calls me) additionally needs the issuer and the
//     trusted-principal allowlist. An empty allowlist is never emitted: it would
//     be a configured-but-unsatisfiable inbound check that locks out every caller.
var trustedCallerEntries = empty(trustedCallerClientId)
  ? {}
  : union(
      {
        CRUFTFREE_CALLER_AUDIENCE_CLIENT_ID: trustedCallerClientId
      },
      empty(trustedCallerPrincipalIds)
        ? {}
        : {
            CRUFTFREE_CALLER_EXPECTED_ISSUER: trustedCallerExpectedIssuer
            CRUFTFREE_CALLER_TRUSTED_PRINCIPAL_IDS: trustedCallerPrincipalIds
          }
    )

// The site module owns the base app settings; this child resource overlays the
// post-deployment keys onto them. baseAppSettings (passed as data from the web-app
// module output) is converted from the name/value array shape into an object with
// toObject(); union() then adds the trusted-caller keys and the late-bound identity
// audiences without removing any base entry. Later arguments win on key collision,
// but the three groups use disjoint key namespaces so no overwrite occurs. No
// self-read of the site own settings is performed (the old self-referential listing
// call was a circular dependency ARM rejects at deploy time).
resource appSettings 'Microsoft.Web/sites/config@2023-12-01' = {
  parent: webApp
  name: 'appsettings'
  properties: union(
    toObject(baseAppSettings, e => e.name, e => e.value),
    trustedCallerEntries,
    identityAudienceSettings
  )
}
